# A HELD Z ANSWERED WITH THE LENS (#120: close combat behind the player, open
# battle on the flat camera), behind `rules.lock_lens`, which is OFF by default
# and ON in `configs/held-z.json`. The same moment as tours/camera_sheet.tour, the
# baseline #120 was asked against, so the two can be held side by side.
#
#   tools/tour.sh tours/held_z.tour --seed=1 --hour=11 --weather=clear:0 --folk=8 --config=held-z
#
# What it proves, from a normal game start, through the real key: a machine in
# front on the flat camera; the lock takes the lens -- asked of the camera's
# `lens` AND its `projection`, which disagreed before the setter existed -- and
# the machine is still in the picture under it; letting go gives the flat camera
# back. The switch is continuous in pitch, so the first frame after the key goes
# down is not a jump; tests/target/test_lock_lens.gd measures that.
coast calm
wait 0.9
spawn runner
wait 0.8
await target_flat 2
shot 01-a-machine-in-front-on-the-flat-camera with mob:runner

hold target
await target 5
await target_lens 3
# The pitch glides home at the lean's rate; give it the time a player would.
await target_lean 5
wait 1.1
shot 02-held-z-the-machine-under-the-lens with mob:runner

release target
await target_flat 3
wait 1.2
shot 03-let-go-the-flat-camera-again with mob:runner
